{{-- Refund & Cancellation Policy — English master version. --}}
<p>This policy explains how payments, the personal account, auto-renewal, cancellation and refunds work for paid products of {{ $legal['name'] }} (GameCon+, the family plan, GameCon+ gifts and server promotion).</p>

<h2>1. How payments work</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Personal account (wallet).</strong> Paid products are bought from your personal account balance (GameCon+ → Account). You top up the account through the third-party donation and payment services listed on the top-up page (for example Donatello, Diaka, Donatik, Buy Me a Coffee or Patreon), quoting the top-up code shown to you.</li>
    <li><strong>Crediting.</strong> Top-ups are credited automatically within minutes where the service supports it, otherwise after manual verification, usually within 24 hours. If a payment arrives without a code or with a different amount, we credit the amount actually received once we can match it to you.</li>
    <li><strong>No card data.</strong> Each service processes the payment under its own terms. We never receive or store your card details.</li>
    <li><strong>Android app.</strong> Purchases in our Android app are made through Google Play Billing; their cancellation and refunds follow Google Play’s policies.</li>
</ul>

<h2>2. Instant access</h2>
<p>Purchases from the account are activated <strong>immediately</strong> and are available on the website and in the app. A gift is credited to the recipient at once; server promotion starts at once or, if all paid slots are taken, at the first free time shown before payment. A new GameCon+ period starts after your current one ends, so no paid days are lost.</p>

<h2>3. Auto-renewal and cancellation</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Optional.</strong> Auto-renewal is turned on only if you choose it when buying GameCon+ or the family plan.</li>
    <li><strong>From the account only.</strong> About 24 hours before the paid period ends, the price is charged from your account balance — never from your card. If the balance is insufficient, we notify you and renew as soon as you top up.</li>
    <li><strong>One-click cancellation.</strong> Turn auto-renewal off at any time in GameCon+ → Account. There are no cancellation fees, penalties or minimum terms, and access continues until the end of the paid period.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Refunds</h2>
<h3>4.1. Unused top-ups — 14 days</h3>
<p>Within <strong>14 days of a top-up</strong> you may ask us to refund the part of that top-up that you have not spent. We refund the amount we actually received, through the original service where it supports refunds or by bank transfer to an account in your name. After 14 days, unspent balance remains available for purchases but is not refundable, except where the law requires otherwise.</p>
<h3>4.2. Purchases — 14 days</h3>
<p>Within <strong>14 days of a purchase</strong> (including a gift or server promotion) you may ask us to cancel it; the price is returned to your account balance and the related access ends. If that money came from a top-up made within the last 14 days, you may then also request it back under section 4.1. This is a voluntary refund window offered in line with EU, UK and US consumer standards; by buying, you request immediate supply of a digital service and, where the law requires, acknowledge that your statutory right of withdrawal may end once the service has been fully supplied.</p>
<h3>4.3. Auto-renewals</h3>
<p>If you forgot to turn auto-renewal off and have not used paid features since the renewal, contact us within 14 days and we will return the renewal price to your account.</p>
<h3>4.4. Technical faults and double charges</h3>
<ul>
    <li>If you were charged twice for the same product or period, or a top-up was credited to the wrong account, we correct it in full regardless of the windows above.</li>
    <li>If a paid feature does not work because of a fault on our side that we cannot fix within a reasonable time, we refund the affected period in full or pro rata.</li>
</ul>
<h3>4.5. Limitations and abuse</h3>
<ul>
    <li>We may refuse a refund where there are signs of abuse: repeated buy-and-refund cycles, refund requests after substantial use of a gift or promotion, using the refund window to obtain paid features for free, fraud, or opening a payment dispute while a refund request is being handled.</li>
    <li>No refund is due if your account was suspended or terminated for a serious breach of the <a href="{{ $legal['site'] }}/terms">Terms of Service</a>, unless the law requires otherwise.</li>
    <li>Changes to the list of paid features (Terms, section 7) are not in themselves grounds for a refund, except where consumer law requires it.</li>
    <li>Fees charged by a donation or payment service are set by that service; we refund what we actually received.</li>
</ul>
<p>Nothing in this policy limits your mandatory statutory rights as a consumer.</p>

<h2>5. How to request a refund</h2>
<p>Write to <a href="mailto:{{ $legal['email'] }}">{{ $legal['email'] }}</a> from the email of your account, with your username, the top-up code or purchase, and the reason. We reply within 3 business days. Approved refunds to the account are immediate; refunds of money depend on the service or bank (usually 5–10 business days).</p>

<h2>6. Payment disputes</h2>
<p>Please contact us before opening a dispute with a donation service or your bank — most issues are solved faster directly. If a payment is reversed, the amount is deducted from your account balance and paid access bought with it may end.</p>

<h2>7. Contact</h2>
<p>{{ $legal['operator'] }} — <a href="mailto:{{ $legal['email'] }}">{{ $legal['email'] }}</a>.</p>
